  "summary": "Framework knitters gathered in Nottingham market place on 11 March 1811 and marched to Arnold, where between about 50 and 63 stocking frames were destroyed in an evening. The attacks on machinery spread through the textile districts of the Midlands, northern England and Flintshire in the years from March 1811 to April 1817.",
